WEBVTT

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:03.560
ano toki umareta no

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:03.560
あのとき生まれたの

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:03.560
I'll softly give you my thoughts

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:09.070
watashi no omoi sotto ageru

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:09.070
私の想いそっとあげる

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:09.070
That were born at that moment

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:14.950
shinjite ite

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:14.950
信じていて

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:14.950
Please believe in them

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.420
deatta hi kara

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.420
出逢った日から

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.420
Since the day when we met

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.670
hajimete no kimochi megutteru

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.670
初めての気持ち巡ってる

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.670
For the first time, I have these feelings, and they go around

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.680
honto no egao hoshii nante

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.680
ホントの笑顔ほしいなんて

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.680
I want your true smile

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:42.560
anata ga oshiete kureta sorao

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:42.560
あなたが教えてくれた空を

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:42.560
I embrace the sky

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:47.690
dakishimete yume o miru

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:47.690
抱きしめて夢をみる

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:47.690
That you told me about and dream

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.520
tooi keredo・・・

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.520
遠いけれど・・・

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.520
It's faraway, but...

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.740
atatakai hikari no kakera

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.740
あたたかい光のかけら

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.740
The fragments of warm light

00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:00.530
kizutsuita hane ni inochi o kureta no

00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:00.530
傷ついた羽根に命をくれたの

00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:00.530
Gave life to my wounded wings

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.950
fureta toki umareta

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.950
触れたとき生まれた

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.950
Born at the moment when we touched

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:08.040
tsuyoi watashi no soba ni

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:08.040
強い私のそばに

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:08.040
Next to me, who is strong

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:13.260
mamoraretai watashi ga nemutte ita no

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:13.260
守られたいわたしが眠っていたの

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:13.260
The me who wants to be protected was asleep

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:18.260
sou unmei kaerareru ne

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:18.260
そう運命変えられるね

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:18.260
That's right, destiny can be changed

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:26.310
futari no koi mezamesasete・・・

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:26.310
ふたりの恋目覚めさせて・・・

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:26.310
Let our love awaken...

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:29.900
{last frame of OP}

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:34.570
Ninth Episode 「You and Me」

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:39.300
Do you want some coffee?

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.470
There's soup as well.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.060
How long do you intend to keep that gloomy face on?

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:52.420
Do you want to karao-

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.430
I guess not.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.220
Are there any games?

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:03.520
This is terrible.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:08.060
Benika-san, is this a job I can even handle?

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.620
I predicted that something like this would happen.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.780
I've failed many times.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:15.490
Do you think I'm angry because of that?

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:17.320
However, in the future...

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:20.410
Could it be you want to leave this job?

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:24.260
I'll do anything I can do.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:28.130
But I feel like this is a job I cannot handle.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:30.610
They even found Samidare Apartment.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:33.130
Wasn't that a matter of time, though?

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:39.080
But I can see that who we're up against is far, far more powerful than I had imagined.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:41.370
I'm sure they're dreadful.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.560
You wanted a big job, right?

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:46.110
You wanted me to recognize you, right?

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:50.870
I can't fight against an enemy I don't know, though.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.390
You mean the Kuhouins?

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:53.990
Murasaki too.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:57.160
Is Murasaki...

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.580
Is she really a Kuhouin?

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.170
I heard that the Kuhouins don't have a girl.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:07.750
Who said that?

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.090
I want to know the truth.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.590
Just who is she?

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:15.460
Murakami Ginko told you?

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:19.560
There wasn't anyone named Murasaki on their family tree.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:21.100
You're a hopeless child.

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:22.810
What is going on?

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:25.060
Murasaki is a child of the Kuhouins.

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:30.240
Her father, Kuhouin Renjou, is the head of the Kuhouins, a plutocratic family.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:31.520
But...

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:33.330
She was...

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:35.810
She was...

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:40.610
She was born from mingling between the Kuhouins themselves.

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:47.550
The Kuhouins can only give birth to children by mingling amongst themselves.

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:49.720
Does that mean...

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:55.580
When women born into the Kuhouin family become adults, they are forced to live in the Inner Sanctuary.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.870
It is a place where noise from the outside cannot even reach.

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:01.700
That is the Inner Sanctuary.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:07.600
In six years, Murasaki would have been treated as an adult.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:09.050
Six years?

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:11.630
She has thirteen years left until she is twenty, though.

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:16.080
In the past, she would have become an adult even earlier.

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:21.240
In six years, she would've been a woman who had already given birth to children by the first and second son of the family.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.720
You mean that siblings get married to each other?

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:26.030
No.

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:29.550
After giving birth, they are not allowed to even become their wives.

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:34.360
They are hidden from society and live within the Inner Sanctuary until they die.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:37.260
In order to hide the fact that they give birth to children from within their family,

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:40.170
the man marries a woman from the outside,

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:44.900
and the married woman becomes the child's mother and raises it.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:48.430
I'm surprised that women from the outside would even come in.

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:51.250
Entrepreneurs want a name for themselves.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.650
Distinguished families need assets.

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:58.690
Well, marriages of convenience used to take place in the past.

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:01.620
But the Kuhouins are slightly different.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:03.700
They have no money problems.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:07.410
In that case, the women are just tools.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:13.300
The married women and Murasaki, a woman born into the Kuhouin family, are all tools.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:17.840
From the very moment Murasaki was born, she became a woman that did not exist.

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:20.580
That's how it is?

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:25.350
From the very beginning, Murasaki was given a fate she could not fight against.

00:05:26.170 --> 00:05:28.260
She has a life where she cannot decide anything for herself.

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:33.830
As I promised Murasaki's true mother, Souju,

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:35.650
I took her outside.

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:39.480
So I wonder, what is she thinking?

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.840
What does she want to do?

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:45.320
Murasaki said she doesn't want to go back to her home.

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:49.870
If that is her will, I want you to help her.

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:53.750
But this job is too big for me.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:56.520
I don't believe that.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:00.880
We haven't lost anything yet, and Murasaki believes in you too.

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:04.860
You've become a man that someone can believe in.

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:09.910
The problem is here on out.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:13.100
I...

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.920
I...

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:19.730
Cannot protect Murasaki?

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:28.570
I...

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:31.830
I will protect Murasaki.

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:38.020
Just as I promised,

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:39.870
I will protect Murasaki.

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:46.010
I'm going to have you two leave the country tomorrow.

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:48.600
I'm having Yayoi go too, so you can contac-

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:49.680
Benika-san.

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:54.350
Could I take Murasaki back to Samidare Apartment before that?

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:56.520
Why?

00:06:57.030 --> 00:07:00.880
She hasn't bidden proper farewell to Tamaki-san and Yamie-san yet.

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:04.140
Even though you know that place is dangerous now?

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:06.950
Farewells are important.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:10.280
I want her to do things like that properly too.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:11.990
No matter what?

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:18.710
If I can't even do something like this, I won't be able to protect Murasaki in the future.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:23.330
In the course of a person's life,

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:26.260
they must make many choices.

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:34.670
Whether that choice is right or wrong, no one knows.

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:43.980
That's why people believe that the choices they make are the right ones.

00:07:45.170 --> 00:07:47.740
You mean to live positively?

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:50.740
There's nothing behind you after all.

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:53.450
Yes.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:57.210
That is why people are interesting.

00:07:57.890 --> 00:07:59.350
They're interesting, you know.

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:03.070
I will believe in my intuition.

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:06.190
And I will believe in you.

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:12.440
I'm against this.

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:13.920
You don't need to do anything.

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:15.990
I can't do that, though.

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:17.730
I won't give them reinforcement either.

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:19.630
Can I ask you a question?

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:20.270
What is it?

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:24.570
Murasaki-san is a person that <i>must </i>be protected, right?

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:25.800
Yes, that's right.

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:26.610
Then why?

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:29.990
Shinkurou said himself that he wanted to do it.

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:32.780
It was rare, but he gave me his own opinion.

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:36.150
I understand that he finds those things important,

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:37.270
but this is a job!

00:08:37.270 --> 00:08:41.430
That's right. It might be impossible for him, depending on whom the Kuhouins send.

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:41.970
But...

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:44.420
Even so, I will believe in Shinkurou.

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:45.670
But then, Murasaki-san will...!

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:47.780
I'm letting Shinkurou do it.

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:49.920
He wants to do it with his own strength.

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:55.220
If it's your order, then.

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:58.120
I'll be taking them to Samidare Apartment then.

00:08:58.120 --> 00:08:59.480
Benika-sama.

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:04.520
If any enemy appears before me, it is my job to fight them, right?

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:06.020
Yes, that's right.

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:10.070
I will return to my usual spot, then.

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:14.320
You're so scattered.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:16.330
Happiness won't come to you.

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:21.710
Well then, we'll be out by morning.

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:23.350
Be as quick as you can about it.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:24.720
Yes.

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:26.700
Yayoi.

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:27.300
Yes.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:29.510
Sorry for being selfish.

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:31.640
I don't mind.

00:09:31.640 --> 00:09:33.840
This is my job, after all.

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:36.180
You just don't understand.

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.360
Rare doesn't mean it's good, you know.

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:39.980
Ah, I understand that.

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:41.840
I like it more raw.

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:43.140
How indecent.

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:43.700
What is?

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:45.480
Stop with that kind of talk.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:47.480
I like it well done.

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:48.520
Right?

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:50.010
Isn't the fire too strong?

00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:52.900
What? Do you have a problem with my hot plate?

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:56.260
No, it's not that, it's just clearly too stro-

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:56.660
Hold it.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:10:00.040
If you like it rare, then we need better meat.

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:03.190
I have some of those Shimofuri ones.

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:04.580
The store worker said not to grill it too much.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:06.040
Are you serious?

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:07.070
Shimofuri?

00:10:07.070 --> 00:10:09.670
I hear these are the tastiest,

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.530
but they're full of fat.

00:10:11.530 --> 00:10:12.460
Do you think they tricked me?

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:13.630
Over half of it is white.

00:10:13.970 --> 00:10:16.950
You were tricked, boy!

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:19.900
That's right, that's some terrible meat!

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:21.530
So I was tricked!

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:24.060
I can't believe they did it just because I always buy cheap meat.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:24.780
How unfortunate!

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:26.380
It's expensive meat, too.

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:30.070
I'll bear with the fat-filled meat and eat it.

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:31.270
I'm fine with it too!

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:34.090
No, you two eat the red meat.

00:10:34.090 --> 00:10:35.200
It's bad for your health.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:36.520
What are you saying?

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:38.280
You're treating us to so much already,

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:39.950
so I can't ask for anything more!

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:45.100
We don't have much of a future left, so we can't eat red meat.

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:47.520
You two youngsters should eat them!

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:50.860
That fat-filled meat is enough for us.

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:54.140
Is it just my imagination, or does this all stink of a lie?

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:56.430
Don't grill it too much!

00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:57.800
Because it's good meat?

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:03.380
Thanks for treating us.

00:11:03.380 --> 00:11:05.200
Take care of the hot plate.

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:07.140
I'll make sure to scrape off all the charred meat.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:08.690
Today was fun too.

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:09.730
See you tomorrow.

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:11.230
Okay.

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:14.960
Well then, good night.

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.890
Good night. {covers both good nights}

00:11:16.890 --> 00:11:18.540
Ah, good night.

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:22.790
That was strange.

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:23.650
What is?

00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:25.240
This welcoming mood.

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:26.750
It's the first time, huh?

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:28.870
Yeah.

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:36.260
It's kind of scary.

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:38.260
Yeah.

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:41.260
I won't cry, though.

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:44.270
I don't want to be like my mother.

00:11:46.650 --> 00:11:47.880
Your mom?

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:51.750
My real mother that gave birth to me.

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:54.690
She was really kind, but weak.

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:56.650
That's why she died.

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:58.060
Murasaki.

00:11:58.060 --> 00:12:00.520
She died and left me behind.

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:03.510
I don't want to die like my mother.

00:12:03.940 --> 00:12:05.120
I want to...

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:07.290
You want to?

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:11.290
I want to live more freely.

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:13.360
You can.

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:14.960
If it's you, I'm sure you can do it.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:18.560
I want to become strong like you and live freely.

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:21.440
I'm still weak.

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:22.800
Shinkurou...

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:27.640
I didn't have confidence in myself, and I had no one to rely on.

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:33.200
That's why I changed myself into someone with a monstrous body.

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:36.050
Monstrous? What is that?

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:40.010
You may see it one day.

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:43.840
Are you strong because you have that?

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:47.070
I got it because I believed that, but...

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:49.800
I always see this one dream.

00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:52.080
Is it a scary dream?

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:59.160
Because of terrorists, not only did my parents die before me, but many other people.

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:04.130
That terrible dream always, always comes to mind.

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:07.460
It's impossible to forget it.

00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:11.260
I can't forget it because I don't have true strength.

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:13.270
I can't forget, either.

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:17.130
I just can't forget about my mother.

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:21.710
But dead people are no longer in this world.

00:13:21.710 --> 00:13:24.620
No matter how much you cry, they won't be found anywhere.

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:27.560
My mother is nowhere.

00:13:27.560 --> 00:13:30.330
And neither are your father and mother.

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:34.710
The people that you and I loved are no longer around.

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:38.250
You and I both became alone.

00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:41.780
But then I met you.

00:13:42.390 --> 00:13:44.230
There'll be two of us if we're together.

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:49.260
You and me, the two of us, huh?

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:51.980
That's why it's not lonely anymore.

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:54.380
Murasaki...

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:57.350
I will protect you.

00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:58.270
Shinkurou?

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:08.190
My mother kissed me a lot.

00:14:08.190 --> 00:14:10.160
When I asked her why,

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:13.660
she said that you kiss people who are important to you.

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:16.440
Important people...

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:21.390
She said, "When you find someone important to you, give them a kiss."

00:14:22.390 --> 00:14:24.910
You're an important person to me.

00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:42.440
Who's there?

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:44.270
It's me.

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:47.340
How did you get in here?

00:14:47.340 --> 00:14:48.910
That's a trade secret.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:51.770
You can't stop smoking?

00:14:51.770 --> 00:14:53.000
It's impossible.

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:57.230
Then you should at least smoke lighter ones.

00:14:57.230 --> 00:15:01.500
Hey, you know why I came, right?

00:15:01.490 --> 00:15:03.100
Yes.

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:05.430
You can't stop it though.

00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:07.340
Ryuuji is already on his way.

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:09.180
Ah, him.

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:12.430
He strongly believes in the laws of the Kuhouins.

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:15.680
Do you believe in them just like your son?

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:19.980
Permitting Ryuuji's actions is my answer.

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:25.950
Even if the daughter you're trying to recover is not the same daughter you once knew?

00:15:27.060 --> 00:15:28.450
What do you mean?

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:34.950
You know, it's not like I wanted her to live outside forever.

00:15:36.530 --> 00:15:38.070
She will change.

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:41.400
She will change along with my precious pupil.

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:42.990
It's futile.

00:15:43.740 --> 00:15:46.370
The laws of the Kuhouins are absolute.

00:15:46.370 --> 00:15:47.990
I'm tired of hearing that.

00:15:47.990 --> 00:15:51.160
I even thought you would do something more.

00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:57.250
My pupil may have unreliable traits to him,

00:15:57.250 --> 00:15:59.270
but he is more reliable than your son.

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:01.370
I see.

00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:04.070
Shall we test him, then?

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:05.890
Let's.

00:16:06.340 --> 00:16:07.240
Would you like to bet on it?

00:16:08.470 --> 00:16:09.950
Very well.

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:51.490
Looking great there.

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:06.800
What is it?

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:19.760
What? Is there a fight?

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:25.560
Wearing shoes inside is prohibited here, you know.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:27.110
Was it?

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:28.360
Not like it makes a difference.

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:30.210
There's a shoe rack downsta-

00:17:31.630 --> 00:17:34.400
Sorry, the shoe rack was full.

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:35.880
There weren't any slippers either.

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:38.790
Think you can forgive us?

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:43.040
She said no.

00:17:56.830 --> 00:17:57.980
Yayoi-san!

00:17:57.980 --> 00:17:59.350
Run away!

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:05.010
Shinkurou!

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:06.810
Murasaki.

00:18:08.320 --> 00:18:09.530
What a filthy room.

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:13.280
I'm amazed you were able to endure this place, Murasaki.

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:15.280
Who are you?

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:19.660
Could you introduce me to him?

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:25.600
That person is Kuhouin Ryuuji.

00:18:26.320 --> 00:18:28.340
My brother.

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:30.400
He is?

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:34.270
How long did you intend to continue living here?

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:36.340
For a while.

00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:37.970
For a while?

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:42.850
You should know very well that it is not allowed.

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:44.720
I understand.

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:49.030
It wasn't your will, but rather that woman Benika's, that misled you.

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:52.780
I don't intend to blame you as your brother.

00:18:53.280 --> 00:18:54.480
Yes.

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:57.780
I know full well that you were unable to go home by yourself.

00:18:57.780 --> 00:18:58.740
That's why I came for you.

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:00.480
What are you saying?

00:19:00.480 --> 00:19:02.840
Murasaki wanted to go outside!

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:04.460
She doesn't want to go back to her home anymore!

00:19:04.460 --> 00:19:05.950
Shinkurou!

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:08.390
Shinkurou, is it?

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:11.270
Just who are you?

00:19:11.270 --> 00:19:13.170
Benika's subordinate or something?

00:19:13.910 --> 00:19:15.440
I'm her pupil.

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:18.190
I'm here to protect Murasaki.

00:19:18.810 --> 00:19:19.940
Protect?

00:19:20.900 --> 00:19:22.710
Is that so, Murasaki?

00:19:23.150 --> 00:19:24.520
Don't worry.

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:26.680
I'll take care of these guys!

00:19:33.180 --> 00:19:34.770
Shinkurou!

00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:37.490
Let me ask you again.

00:19:37.910 --> 00:19:43.410
Murasaki, tell me what you are supposed to do as a Kuhouin woman.

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:46.910
You don't need to do anything, Murasaki! I'll...

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:50.420
I'll protect you!

00:19:58.540 --> 00:19:59.720
Shinkurou...

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:04.850
Answer me, Murasaki.

00:20:05.410 --> 00:20:08.400
I want to confirm your will.

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:10.060
I...

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:11.980
Depending on your answer...

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:13.730
He may lose his life.

00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:22.840
Murasaki...

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:25.770
Answer.

00:20:26.290 --> 00:20:31.720
As a Kuhouin woman,

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:34.420
I am to give birth to Kuhouin children.

00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:36.420
And?

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:40.290
For that purpose, I am fated to enter the Inner Sanctuary,

00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:45.090
and to live for the Kuhouins.

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:47.500
No, Murasaki.

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:49.390
You don't want to do that, do you?

00:20:50.960 --> 00:20:55.340
And for that purpose, what must you do now, Murasaki?

00:20:56.490 --> 00:20:59.490
I have to return to the Inner Sanctuary.

00:20:59.490 --> 00:21:01.310
Murasaki!

00:21:01.310 --> 00:21:03.410
No, what's wrong?

00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:06.880
It's okay, Shinkurou.

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:09.370
This is farewell.

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:12.400
Why are you giving up?

00:21:13.130 --> 00:21:14.630
I...

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:20.360
Cease your foolish actions.

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:23.790
It's just as Murasaki explained herself.

00:21:24.410 --> 00:21:27.860
She is a woman fated to give birth to my children, as I am her brother.

00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:30.850
Shinkurou...

00:21:32.090 --> 00:21:34.060
Murasaki...

00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:38.960
Farewell.

00:21:41.260 --> 00:21:42.530
Murasaki...

00:21:43.520 --> 00:21:47.240
Thank you for everything.

00:21:48.270 --> 00:21:51.940
Murasaki, walk with your own will.

00:21:52.530 --> 00:21:56.600
Prove that you have accepted your fate by yourself.

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:04.010
Murasaki!

00:22:06.940 --> 00:22:08.890
It was fun.

00:22:16.550 --> 00:22:19.110
Murasaki...

00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:06.820
sonna ni asette sa nani mo kamo shiritai to omowanaide

00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:06.820
そんなに焦ってさ何もかも知りたいと思わないで

00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:06.820
Rushing so much, don't think that you want to know everything.

00:23:02.520 --> 00:23:02.560
{last frame of Kimono}

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:12.950
kimi dake no RIZUMU de tokiakashite ikeba ii

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:12.950
君だけのリズムで解き明かしていけばいい

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:12.950
Just figure it out in your own rhythm.

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:16.540
demo ne chotto dake isoide sagashita houga ii kamo ne

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:16.540
でもねちょっとだけ急いで探した方がいいかもね

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:16.540
But it's probably better to rush and search just a little.

00:23:16.540 --> 00:23:19.540
sunadokei to isshou ni SARASARA ochite yuku genjitsu to

00:23:16.540 --> 00:23:19.540
砂時計と一緒にサラサラ落ちてゆく現実と

00:23:16.540 --> 00:23:19.540
Along with the reality that gently falls with the hourglass.

00:23:19.910 --> 00:23:23.040
futte kuru mirai kasanaru shunkan ichido daketo

00:23:19.910 --> 00:23:23.040
降ってくる未来重なる瞬間一度だけと

00:23:19.910 --> 00:23:23.040
The moment the raining future overlaps occurs only once.

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:25.960
sou kizuita

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:25.960
そう気付いた

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:25.960
I realized that.

00:23:26.340 --> 00:23:33.090
hatenaku toumei na jiyuu ni iro o tsukete ikou It's my way

00:23:26.340 --> 00:23:33.090
果てなく透明な自由に色をつけていこう It's my way

00:23:26.340 --> 00:23:33.090
Let's color the endlessly transparent freedom: it's my way.

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:39.230
kousa suru IMEEJI kanji nagara sa

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:39.230
交差するイメージ感じながらさ

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:39.230
As we feel the crossing image.

00:23:39.640 --> 00:23:46.360
kimi no yuku michi no kiseki ni sotto yorisoinagara we can take

00:23:39.640 --> 00:23:46.360
君の行く道の軌跡にそっと寄り添いながら we can take

00:23:39.640 --> 00:23:46.360
As we quietly snuggle up to the miracle on your path: we can take

00:23:46.650 --> 00:23:52.150
betsubetsu no RAIN tadotte iku yo

00:23:46.650 --> 00:23:52.150
別々のラインたどっていくよ

00:23:46.650 --> 00:23:52.150
Tracing separate lines.

